{"id": "civil_comments/test/28151", "source": "civil_comments", "primitive": "noul", "split": "test", "state": "\"Hello Ken!\\n\\nThere is nothing in the Charter about a right to buy a house. Your attempt is laughable to try to paint, as a human rights violation (roll eyes), a restriction against foreigners from buying property. Such restrictions exist, legally, in many countries in the world.\\n\\nEvidence for the scope of the Quebec Investor Immigrant Program? Are you kidding? You can read about that right on the official Quebec Government webpages, try googling \\\"The Quebec Immigrant Investor Program\\\" and \\\"program leading to Canada immigration for high net worth candidates\\\". Also online you can try googling news headlines such as \\\"Quebec immigrant program increases in popularity … with 'downsides' for B.C.\\\", where the most recently tabulated year was between 5,000 and 6,000 immigrants accepted through the program.\\n\\nIt is laughable that you call this a housing bubble soon to pop. By that talk, Vancouver has been in a \\\"housing bubble\\\" (roll eyes) for decades!\"", "question": "{\"type\": \"noul\", \"instructions\": \"Is this comment toxic?\", \"criteria\": {\"true\": \"Rude, disrespectful, or likely to make someone leave the discussion.\", \"false\": \"Civil, even if critical or blunt.\"}}", "label": "0", "soft_label": "0.0", "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"google/civil_comments\", \"license\": \"cc0-1.0\", \"domain\": \"safety\", \"task_family\": \"toxicity\", \"hf_config\": \"default\", \"severe_toxicity\": 0.0}"}
{"id": "civil_comments/test/36237", "source": "civil_comments", "primitive": "noul", "split": "test", "state": "\"I appreciate that Mr. Rutenberg is in journalistic turmoil about how to cover a nominee he hates and believes is dangerous.  But he loses me early on as he decries the lost balance in journalistic coverage.  If Mr. Rutenberg, his editors, and the people who decide what gets covered on the 24 hour news cycle had given as much time to Trump's opponents during the primaries as they gave to the daily crazy junk Trump spewed today, they probably wouldn't be so tormented now.  \\n\\nHonestly, how much time does it take to report on just one thing said  by Bush, Cruz, Rubio, Kasich, Carson, Christie, Fiorina, Graham, Paul, et. al?  Seriously, the major newspapers and networks couldn't send one newbie journalism grad to cover each one and then print/put on the air one thing they each said in a 24 hour news cycle?  It's not like candidates have a different speech every day.  The media could have spent a little bit of time telling Americans what Trump's opponents were saying.\\n\\nCrocodile tears.\"", "question": "{\"type\": \"noul\", \"instructions\": \"Is this comment toxic?\", \"criteria\": {\"true\": \"Rude, disrespectful, or likely to make someone leave the discussion.\", \"false\": \"Civil, even if critical or blunt.\"}}", "label": "0", "soft_label": "0.4000000059604645", "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"google/civil_comments\", \"license\": \"cc0-1.0\", \"domain\": \"safety\", \"task_family\": \"toxicity\", \"hf_config\": \"default\", \"severe_toxicity\": 0.0}"}
